#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:1
msgid "Decode According to the WHATWG Encoding Standard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:3
msgid ""
"This package provides a thin layer on top of [iconv-"
"lite](https://github.com/ashtuchkin/iconv-lite) which makes it expose "
"some of the same primitives as the [Encoding "
"Standard](https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:25
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:27
msgid ""
"`decode(uint8Array, fallbackEncodingName)`: performs the "
"[decode](https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#decode) algorithm (in which "
"any BOM will override the passed fallback encoding), and returns the "
"resulting string"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:28
msgid ""
"`labelToName(label)`: performs the [get an "
"encoding](https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-encoding-get) "
"algorithm and returns the resulting encoding's name, or `null` for "
"failure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:29
msgid ""
"`isSupported(name)`: returns whether the encoding is one of [the "
"encodings](https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#names-and-labels) of the "
"Encoding Standard, _and_ is an encoding that this package can decode (via"
" iconv-lite)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:30
msgid ""
"`getBOMEncoding(uint8Array)`: sniffs the first 2–3 bytes of the supplied "
"`Uint8Array`, returning one of the encoding names `\"UTF-8\"`, `\"UTF-"
"16LE\"`, or `\"UTF-16BE\"` if the appropriate BOM is present, or `null` "
"if no BOM is present"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:32
msgid "Unsupported encodings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:34
msgid ""
"Since we rely on iconv-lite, we are limited to support only the encodings"
" that they support. Currently we are missing support for:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:36
msgid "ISO-2022-JP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:37
msgid "ISO-8859-8-I"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:38
msgid "replacement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:39
msgid "x-mac-cyrillic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:40
msgid "x-user-defined"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:42
msgid ""
"Passing these encoding names will return `false` when calling "
"`isSupported`, and passing any of the possible labels for these encodings"
" to `labelToName` will return `null`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:44
msgid "Credits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:46
msgid ""
"This package was originally based on the excellent work of "
"[@nicolashenry](https://github.com/nicolashenry), [in "
"jsdom](https://github.com/tmpvar/jsdom/blob/7ce11776ce161e8d5921a7a183585327400f786b/lib/jsdom/living/helpers/encoding.js)."
" It has since been pulled out into this separate package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:48
msgid "Alternatives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-encoding_README.md:50
msgid ""
"If you are looking for a JavaScript implementation of the Encoding "
"Standard's `TextEncoder` and `TextDecoder` APIs, you'll want "
"[@inexorabletash](https://github.com/inexorabletash)'s [text-"
"encoding](https://github.com/inexorabletash/text-encoding) package. "
"Node.js also has them [built-"
"in](https://nodejs.org/dist/latest/docs/api/globals.html#globals_textdecoder)."
msgstr ""

